-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ד/1 — העסקת עו"ה עובדי בעלויות בחט"ב הרשמיות בהתאם
-- לרפורמת "אופק חדש" לשנה"ל תשע"ד (27.11.2013)
-- Owners' teaching employees in the official junior high schools under Ofek
-- Hadash in תשע"ד: the placement process and who does what (principal,
-- owner, Ministry), the conditions of joining (new and existing teachers,
-- non-academics, interns, substitutes), the work-week structure (hours,
-- minimum and maximum positions, mothers, age hours, principals and
-- deputies), the salary advance until the grade is set, and the time clock.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `חוזר תשע"ד/1 עובדי בעלויות בחט"ב באופק חדש תשע"ד`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, title, dates and addressee; no rule.

DECLARE `role in the junior high` IS ONE OF
    `a teacher`
    `an intern`
    `a principal`
    `a first deputy principal`
    `a second or later deputy`

@desc An owner's teaching employee in an official junior high school, as this circular asks about them.
DECLARE `junior-high teacher` HAS
    `role`                              IS A `role in the junior high`
    `prior teaching seniority recognised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc whether teaching seniority was ever recognised, from an employer outside the civil service or within it — an internship year, army or national service in teaching excepted
    `seniority years`                   IS A NUMBER  @desc teaching seniority in years, as the Ministry determines it
    `academic`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc holds an academic degree
    `teaching certificate`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `completed internship successfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed the undertaking`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc signed the undertaking to complete an academic degree (annex א)
    `junior-high position`              IS A NUMBER  @desc the share of a full position held in the junior high
    `total position`                    IS A NUMBER  @desc the position held in all schools together
    `number of schools`                 IS A NUMBER
    `age`                               IS A NUMBER
    `paramedical`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc a paramedical teaching employee as defined in the Director-General's circular תשנ"ט/10(א)
    `entitled to a mother's position`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc a mother employed in all her positions above 79% (4.3.1)
    `school in the reform`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc the junior high's entry into Ofek Hadash was approved by the Pedagogical Administration
    `substitute in weekly hours`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc a substitute employed in weekly hours (not single hours)
    `placed in the placement system`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc the principal placed the employee in the placement system (Mashkit) as required

§§ `1. מבוא`

-- akn:art_1/p1 Background: the Ofek Hadash collective agreement was signed on 25.12.2008; no rule.
-- akn:art_1/p7 States the circular's purpose; no rule.
-- akn:art_1/p8 Background: joining requires the owner's data, so actions are split between the principal and the owner — section 2.

-- ¶2-¶3: in תשע"ד the reform is applied in all official junior highs whose
-- entry the Pedagogical Administration approved. ¶4: to state employees and
-- owners' employees alike. ¶5: only to the junior-high fraction, never to
-- the upper division.
@ref akn:art_1/p2 akn:art_1/p3 akn:art_1/p4 akn:art_1/p5
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position the reform governs` t IS
    IF t's `school in the reform` OR `a new teacher meeting the thresholds` t
    THEN t's `junior-high position`
    ELSE 0

-- ¶6: the Ministry alone approves joining and sets the Ofek Hadash grade
-- ("conversion"), and, as before, the education grade and the seniority —
-- which is why they are inputs here, never computed.
DECLARE `ofek action` IS ONE OF
    `approve joining and set the grade`
    `place the owners' employees in the placement system`
    `set a timetable by the Ofek work week`
    `update and approve the placements`
    `reject the placements of inactive teachers`
    `locate the teachers who meet the conditions`
    `send updated data to open or update a file`
    `employ by the Ofek work week`
    `send the salary interface to the conversion centre`
    `pay salary by the grade from joining`
    `pay salary advances`
    `pay the salary due retroactively and deduct the advances`
    `apply to the district treasury for union hours`
    `check each teacher's joining`
    `compute the school's Ofek profile`
    `reimburse the owner`
    `install a time clock`
    `report working hours by the clock`
    `pay and deduct by the clock reports`
    `follow up the undertaking`
    `send the request to the conditions-of-service department`

@ref akn:art_1/p6
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `ofek action`
DECIDE `only the Ministry sets joining and grade` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MAY   `approve joining and set the grade`

§§ `2. תחומי אחריות ביישום הרפורמה`

-- ¶1-¶3: the process begins with the principal placing the owners'
-- employees in the placement system; the data serve the Ministry for
-- rights, joining, promotion, union-hours accounts and the profile. ¶4: the
-- principal is responsible for the report and its accuracy. ¶5: the
-- placement includes every owner's employee teaching in the junior high,
-- hours beyond the standard included.
@ref akn:art_2/p1 akn:art_2/p2 akn:art_2/p3 akn:art_2/p4 akn:art_2/p5
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `ofek action`
DECIDE `the principal places every owner's employee` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `place the owners' employees in the placement system`

-- akn:art_2/p6 Background: the system created special positions for owners' employees automatically, with the status "requires treatment", from last year's report; no rule.

-- ¶7: new teachers not reported last year may be entered in the placement
-- system only by the school's supervisor.
DECLARE `who enters a placement` IS ONE OF
    `the principal`
    `the supervisor only`

@ref akn:art_2/p7
GIVEN `reported last year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `who enters a placement`
DECIDE `who may enter a new teacher` `reported last year` IS
    IF `reported last year` THEN `the principal` ELSE `the supervisor only`

-- ¶8: teachers reported in תשע"ג are joined automatically when the
-- placements are carried to תשע"ד, if they meet the criteria. ¶9: new
-- teachers, or veterans not joined, who meet the conditions are joined by
-- the collection headquarters at the request of the principal or the owner.
-- ¶10: joining is completed before the placement.
@ref akn:art_2/p8 akn:art_2/p9 akn:art_2/p10
GIVEN `reported in תשע"ג` IS A BOOLEAN, `meets the criteria` IS A BOOLEAN, `requested by the principal or owner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `joined to Ofek Hadash for תשע"ד` `reported in תשע"ג` `meets the criteria` `requested by the principal or owner` IF
    `meets the criteria` AND (`reported in תשע"ג` OR `requested by the principal or owner`)

-- ¶11 and א-ג: the principal (א) sets a timetable by the Ofek week; (ב)
-- updates and approves the placements — roles, position, weekly hours, kind
-- of standard hours — every position as an owner's position not against the
-- standard; (ג) rejects the placements of teachers not active in תשע"ד.
-- Saving the placements is a threshold condition for seniority, profile and
-- reimbursement (ג ¶2); no status or approval is needed (¶3); an owner's
-- employee's placement is approved on the update (¶4).
-- akn:art_2/p11 Heading: "the junior-high principal will do the following"; the rules are its items.
@ref akn:art_2__para_a akn:art_2__para_b akn:art_2__para_b/p2 akn:art_2__para_c akn:art_2__para_c/p2 akn:art_2__para_c/p3 akn:art_2__para_c/p4
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `ofek action`
DECIDE `the principal's tasks` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `set a timetable by the Ofek work week`
    HENCE (PARTY `the school principal`
           MUST  `update and approve the placements`
           HENCE (PARTY `the school principal`
                  MUST  `reject the placements of inactive teachers`))

-- ג ¶5-¶7: requests to employ an owner's employee above 106% of a position,
-- or below the minimum (existing teacher 1/3, new teacher 1/2), go from the
-- principal or owner to the conditions-of-service department at the senior
-- personnel division; for one employed by both the State and an owner, to
-- the district personnel officers.
-- akn:art_2__para_c/p5 Heading: "approval of employment above 100% / below the minimum"; the rules follow.
DECLARE `approver` IS ONE OF
    `the conditions-of-service department at headquarters`
    `the district personnel officers`
    `the district personnel managers`
    `the head of the senior personnel division`
    `no approval needed`

@ref akn:art_2__para_c/p6 akn:art_2__para_c/p7
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`, `also employed by the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `approver`
DECIDE `who approves under 2ג` t `also employed by the State` IS
    IF     t's `total position` GREATER THAN 106%
        OR (`an existing teacher` t AND t's `total position` LESS THAN 1 DIVIDED BY 3)
        OR (`a new teacher` t AND t's `total position` LESS THAN 1 DIVIDED BY 2)
    THEN IF `also employed by the State`
         THEN `the district personnel officers`
         ELSE `the conditions-of-service department at headquarters`
    ELSE `no approval needed`

-- ג ¶8 and 1-4: the owner (1) locates the junior-high owners' employees who
-- meet the joining conditions (section 3); (2) sends the district's
-- personnel managers the data to open or update their files; (3) employs
-- them by the Ofek work week (section 4); (4) to set an initial grade,
-- sends the salary-data interface to the Ofek conversion centre (Unique),
-- by the finance division's instructions (annex ב), from which the Ministry
-- sets the grade (¶2); a teacher not placed cannot be converted or promoted
-- (¶3). (5) pays salary by the grade and the agreement from joining.
-- akn:art_2__para_c/p8 Heading: "the owner will do the following"; the rules are its items.
@ref akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_1 akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_2 akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_3 akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_4 akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_4/p2 akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_5
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `ofek action`
DECIDE `the owner's tasks` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `locate the teachers who meet the conditions`
    HENCE (PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
           MUST  `send updated data to open or update a file`
           HENCE (PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
                  MUST  `employ by the Ofek work week`
                  HENCE (PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
                         MUST  `send the salary interface to the conversion centre`
                         HENCE (PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
                                MUST  `approve joining and set the grade`
                                HENCE (PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
                                       MUST  `pay salary by the grade from joining`)))))

@ref akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_4/p3
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `can be converted and promoted` t IF
    t's `placed in the placement system`

-- (6): at the start of the year, until a grade is set, the owner pays
-- salary advances (section 5); once it is set, it pays the salary due
-- retroactively and deducts the advances.
@ref akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_6
GIVEN `grade set` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `ofek action`
DECIDE `advances until the grade` `grade set` IS
    IF `grade set`
    THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `pay the salary due retroactively and deduct the advances`
    ELSE PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `pay salary advances`
         HENCE (PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
                MUST  `pay the salary due retroactively and deduct the advances`)

-- (7): hours asked for a salary union against the institution's standard
-- need the district treasury's approval, by the rules and subject to unused
-- standard; the principal's report is a threshold, not an approval (¶2).
-- The accounts follow the manual report (list ב, ¶3) in two parts — Ofek
-- Hadash teachers and pre-reform teachers (¶4-¶6); the frontal hours of
-- both are checked against the standard (¶7); for approved frontal hours of
-- Ofek teachers, individual and stay hours are reimbursed too (¶8).
@ref akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_7 akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_7/p2 akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_7/p3 akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_7/p4 akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_7/p5 akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_7/p6 akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_7/p7
GIVEN `frontal hours asked` IS A NUMBER, `unused standard` IS A NUMBER, `approved by the district treasury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `union hours approved` `frontal hours asked` `unused standard` `approved by the district treasury` IS
    IF `approved by the district treasury` THEN min `frontal hours asked` `unused standard` ELSE 0

@ref akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_7/p8
GIVEN `approved frontal hours` IS A NUMBER, `under Ofek Hadash` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `individual and stay hours reimbursed with them` `approved frontal hours` `under Ofek Hadash` IF
    `under Ofek Hadash` AND `approved frontal hours` GREATER THAN 0

-- ¶9 and 1-3: the Ministry checks each owner's employee and decides
-- joining; computes the school's Ofek profile; and reimburses the owner for
-- the approved hours by Ofek terms — accurately only if the placement
-- system follows the Ofek week and the salary interface reached the
-- conversion centre.
-- akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_7/p9 Heading: "the Ministry will do the following"; the rules are its items.
@ref akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_7__cls_1 akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_7__cls_2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `ofek action`
DECIDE `the Ministry's tasks` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `check each teacher's joining`
    HENCE (PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
           MUST  `compute the school's Ofek profile`)

@ref akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_7__cls_3
GIVEN `placement updated to the Ofek week` IS A BOOLEAN, `salary interface sent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ministry can reimburse the owner` `placement updated to the Ofek week` `salary interface sent` IF
    `placement updated to the Ofek week` AND `salary interface sent`

§§ `3. תנאי ההצטרפות`

-- akn:art_3__para_3-1 Heading of 3.1 ("הגדרות"); the definitions follow.

-- 3.1.1: a new teacher has never had teaching seniority recognised, from an
-- employer outside the civil service or within it — an internship year,
-- army or national service in teaching excepted. 3.1.2: an existing
-- teacher is one who is not new.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_3-1-1
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a new teacher` t IF
    NOT t's `prior teaching seniority recognised`

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_3-1-2
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing teacher` t IF
    NOT `a new teacher` t

-- akn:art_3__para_3-2 Heading of 3.2 (existing teachers in a junior high joined to the reform); the rules follow.

-- 3.2.1: in a junior high where the reform is applied every teacher
-- is employed under it — except teachers who are not academics, and
-- substitutes "in certain conditions" (read by 3.6: a substitute takes the
-- terms of the teacher replaced).
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employed under the reform by 3.2.1` t IF
        t's `school in the reform`
    AND t's `academic`
    AND NOT t's `substitute in weekly hours`

-- akn:art_3__para_3-3 Heading of 3.3 (teachers who are not academics); the rules follow.

-- 3.3.1: a non-academic with up to 27 years' seniority (inclusive) must
-- sign an undertaking to complete an academic degree within 4 years of
-- signing; until signed, not joined. The form is annex א; it goes to the
-- district personnel office. 3.3.2: a non-academic with 28 years and more
-- need not sign and is employed under the reform in any case.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-1
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must sign the undertaking` t IF
    (NOT t's `academic`) AND t's `seniority years` AT MOST 27

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-2
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employed under the reform without an undertaking` t IF
    (NOT t's `academic`) AND t's `seniority years` AT LEAST 28

GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a non-academic joins` t IF
       `employed under the reform without an undertaking` t
    OR (`must sign the undertaking` t AND t's `signed the undertaking`)

-- F-2012-13_tashag_03-d: the two bands meet at 27 and 28; a seniority
-- between them (27.5 years) is in neither.
`27.5 years of seniority is in neither band of 3.3` MEANS
    (NOT (27.5 AT MOST 27)) AND (NOT (27.5 AT LEAST 28))
#ASSERT `27.5 years of seniority is in neither band of 3.3`

-- F-2012-13_tashag_03-b: 3.2.1 excepts non-academics from employment under
-- the reform; 3.3.2 employs a non-academic of 28 years "in any case" under
-- it, and 3.3.1 joins one who signed.
`a non-academic with thirty years` MEANS
    `junior-high teacher` WITH
        `role`                               IS `a teacher`
        `prior teaching seniority recognised` IS TRUE
        `seniority years`                    IS 30
        `academic`                           IS FALSE
        `teaching certificate`               IS TRUE
        `completed internship successfully`  IS TRUE
        `signed the undertaking`             IS FALSE
        `junior-high position`               IS 1
        `total position`                     IS 1
        `number of schools`                  IS 1
        `age`                                IS 56
        `paramedical`                        IS FALSE
        `entitled to a mother's position`    IS FALSE
        `school in the reform`               IS TRUE
        `substitute in weekly hours`         IS FALSE
        `placed in the placement system`     IS TRUE

`3.2.1 and 3.3.2 disagree on a non-academic of 28 years and more` MEANS
    NOT (`employed under the reform by 3.2.1` `a non-academic with thirty years`
         EQUALS `employed under the reform without an undertaking` `a non-academic with thirty years`)
#ASSERT `3.2.1 and 3.3.2 disagree on a non-academic of 28 years and more`

-- 3.3.3: the undertaking is followed up.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `ofek action`
DECIDE `the undertaking is followed up` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `follow up the undertaking`

-- 3.3.4: a teacher who presents the degree within 4 years of joining the
-- reform's terms, or of תשע"ד (the earlier), gets salary differences from
-- the joining date; later, the teacher is converted to the academics'
-- salary without differences. Years are counted from 1 September of the
-- anchor year (תשע"ד = 2013).
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-4
GIVEN `joining year` IS A NUMBER @desc the calendar year in whose September the teacher joined the reform's terms
      `degree year` IS A NUMBER @desc when the degree certificates were presented, on the same scale: the calendar year of the September a school year opens, plus the fraction of that school year (2016.5 = half way through the school year that opened in September 2016)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to salary differences` `joining year` `degree year` IF
    `degree year` MINUS min `joining year` 2013 AT MOST 4

-- 3.3.5: in very exceptional cases a teacher who lacks a criterion (a
-- teaching certificate, a degree or the minimum position) may apply, with
-- the supervisor's recommendation and reasons, to the head of the senior
-- personnel division, who decides.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-5
GIVEN `approved by the division head` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `joins by exception` `approved by the division head` IF
    `approved by the division head`

-- akn:art_3__para_3-4 Heading of 3.4 (new teachers); the rule follows.

-- 3.4.1: every new teacher in a junior high is employed under Ofek Hadash
-- even where the school is not in the reform — provided they hold a
-- teaching certificate and a degree, passed the internship, and have no
-- prior teaching seniority.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4__subpara_3-4-1
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a new teacher meeting the thresholds` t IF
        `a new teacher` t
    AND t's `teaching certificate`
    AND t's `academic`
    AND t's `completed internship successfully`

-- akn:art_3__para_3-5 Heading of 3.5 (interns); the rules follow.

-- 3.5.1: interns are employed only under the reform; the internship year
-- counts only at a third of a position or more. 3.5.2: at most two years,
-- in which the degree and certificate must be completed, or no further
-- employment under the reform.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-1
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internship year is recognised` t IF
    t's `role` EQUALS `an intern` AND t's `junior-high position` AT LEAST 1 DIVIDED BY 3

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-2
GIVEN `years of internship` IS A NUMBER, `completed degree and certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an intern may go on under the reform` `years of internship` `completed degree and certificate` IF
    `years of internship` AT MOST 2 OR `completed degree and certificate`

-- 3.5.3: the internship does not count for salary seniority or the
-- minimum time to a grade; it counts for tenure, the jubilee grant and
-- recuperation.
DECLARE `purpose of seniority` IS ONE OF
    `salary seniority`
    `minimum time to promotion`
    `tenure`
    `jubilee grant`
    `recuperation`

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-3 akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-3/p2
GIVEN p IS A `purpose of seniority`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internship counts for` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `tenure`        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `jubilee grant` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `recuperation`  THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- 3.5.4: an intern with seniority greater than 1 on joining is converted
-- like any veteran.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-4
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an intern converted like a veteran` t IF
    t's `role` EQUALS `an intern` AND t's `seniority years` GREATER THAN 1

-- 3.6 (printed under 3.5.4, ¶2-¶3): a substitute in weekly hours (in the reform or not) takes the terms
-- of the teacher replaced.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-4/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-4/p3
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`, `the replaced teacher is under the reform` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a substitute is under the reform` t `the replaced teacher is under the reform` IF
    t's `substitute in weekly hours` AND `the replaced teacher is under the reform`

§§ `4. מבנה שבוע העבודה`

-- 4.1.1: a full position is 5 working days, also in six-day schools.
@ref akn:art_4/p1
`working days of a full position` MEANS 5

-- 4.1.2: a teacher who is not a principal or first deputy works 36 hours:
-- 23 frontal, 4 individual, 9 stay. A paramedical teacher: 23, 3, 10.
DECLARE `work week` HAS
    `frontal hours`    IS A NUMBER
    `individual hours` IS A NUMBER
    `stay hours`       IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_4/p2
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the full-position work week` t IS
    IF t's `paramedical`
    THEN `work week` 23 3 10
    ELSE `work week` 23 4 9

GIVEN w IS A `work week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `total hours` w IS
    w's `frontal hours` PLUS w's `individual hours` PLUS w's `stay hours`

-- 4.1.3: a part position takes each kind of hour in proportion (the tables
-- are on the web).
@ref akn:art_4/p3
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the work week for the position` t IS
    `work week` WITH
        `frontal hours`    IS (`the full-position work week` t)'s `frontal hours` TIMES t's `junior-high position`
        `individual hours` IS (`the full-position work week` t)'s `individual hours` TIMES t's `junior-high position`
        `stay hours`       IS (`the full-position work week` t)'s `stay hours` TIMES t's `junior-high position`

-- 4.1.4: at most two schools, and no more than 100% in all.
@ref akn:art_4/p4
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within the limits of 4.1.4` t IF
    t's `number of schools` AT MOST 2 AND t's `total position` AT MOST 1

-- 4.1.5: an existing teacher's position is not below 33%, a new teacher's
-- not below 50%; a teacher employed below a third of a position in Ofek
-- Hadash gets no credit for the period towards the minimum time to
-- promotion.
@ref akn:art_4/p5
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the minimum position` t IS
    IF `a new teacher` t THEN 50% ELSE 33%

GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the period counts towards promotion` t IF
    t's `junior-high position` AT LEAST 1 DIVIDED BY 3

-- ¶6 and 4.2: above a full position only in special cases, with approval
-- in advance, for teachers who are not principals or first deputies, and
-- in frontal hours only. 4.2.1: as a rule up to 100%. 4.2.2: approval in
-- exceptional cases by the system's needs and the criteria 4.2.2.1-5.
-- akn:art_4/p7 Heading of 4.2 ("employment above 100% in the reform"); the rules follow.
DECLARE `extra-hours request` HAS
    `subject in demand`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc science, English, mathematics, special education or physical education (4.2.2.1)
    `shortage in the area`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc 4.2.2.2
    `remote locality`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc 4.2.2.3: a school in a remote locality with difficulty absorbing teachers
    `extra hours all frontal`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc 4.2.2.4
    `hours a day`              IS A NUMBER  @desc total working hours a day (frontal, individual, stay)
    `hours a week`             IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_4/p6 akn:art_4/p8 akn:art_4/p9 akn:art_4/p10 akn:art_4/p11 akn:art_4/p12 akn:art_4/p13 akn:art_4/p14
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`, r IS AN `extra-hours request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be approved above a full position` t r IF
        NOT t's `role` EQUALS `a principal`
    AND NOT t's `role` EQUALS `a first deputy principal`
    AND (r's `subject in demand` OR r's `shortage in the area` OR r's `remote locality`)
    AND r's `extra hours all frontal`
    AND r's `hours a day` AT MOST 8.5
    AND r's `hours a week` AT MOST 42

-- 4.2.3: approved by the system's needs by the district personnel
-- managers. 4.2.4: beyond 42 hours, to the head of the senior personnel
-- division with reasons.
@ref akn:art_4/p15 akn:art_4/p16
GIVEN r IS AN `extra-hours request`
GIVETH AN `approver`
DECIDE `who approves` r IS
    IF r's `hours a week` GREATER THAN 42
    THEN `the head of the senior personnel division`
    ELSE `the district personnel managers`

-- akn:art_4/p17 Heading of 4.3 (a mother); the rules follow.

-- 4.3.1: a mother's position by the takanon: employed above 79% in all her
-- positions. 4.3.2: she may take one frontal hour and one stay hour off the
-- week (the structure is on the web, ¶2-¶3).
@ref akn:art_4/p18
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a mother's position applies` t IF
    t's `entitled to a mother's position` AND t's `total position` GREATER THAN 79%

@ref akn:art_4/p18
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the mother's work week` t IS
    `work week` WITH
        `frontal hours`    IS (`the full-position work week` t)'s `frontal hours` MINUS 1
        `individual hours` IS (`the full-position work week` t)'s `individual hours`
        `stay hours`       IS (`the full-position work week` t)'s `stay hours` MINUS 1

-- akn:art_4/p19 Points to the mother's work-week table on the web; no rule.
-- akn:art_4__para_4-4 Heading of 4.4 (age hours); the rules follow.
-- akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-1 Says the age of entitlement is unchanged from before the reform; the ages themselves are those of 4.4.2-4.4.4.

-- 4.4.2: existing and new teachers "aged 50-55": 2 frontal hours off (base
-- 34). 4.4.3: existing teachers "aged 55 and above": 3 frontal and 1
-- individual off (base 32). 4.4.4: new teachers 55 and above: 2 frontal
-- (base 34). Part positions in proportion.
DECLARE `age band` HAS
    `band from age`     IS A NUMBER
    `band to age`       IS A NUMBER
    `for existing`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `for new`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `frontal off`       IS A NUMBER
    `individual off`    IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-2 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-3 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4
`the age bands as printed` MEANS
    LIST `age band` 50 55  TRUE  TRUE  2 0,
         `age band` 55 999 TRUE  FALSE 3 1,
         `age band` 55 999 FALSE TRUE  2 0

GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A LIST OF `age band`
DECIDE `the age bands for` t IS
    filter (GIVEN b YIELD     t's `age` AT LEAST b's `band from age`
                          AND t's `age` AT MOST b's `band to age`
                          AND ((`an existing teacher` t AND b's `for existing`) OR (`a new teacher` t AND b's `for new`)))
           `the age bands as printed`

-- F-2012-13_tashag_03-a: an existing teacher aged 55 is "aged 50-55" and
-- "aged 55 and above": 2 hours off (base 34) and 4 hours off (base 32).
`an existing teacher of 55 gets two age bands` MEANS
    count (`the age bands for` (`junior-high teacher` WITH
        `role`                               IS `a teacher`
        `prior teaching seniority recognised` IS TRUE
        `seniority years`                    IS 25
        `academic`                           IS TRUE
        `teaching certificate`               IS TRUE
        `completed internship successfully`  IS TRUE
        `signed the undertaking`             IS FALSE
        `junior-high position`               IS 1
        `total position`                     IS 1
        `number of schools`                  IS 1
        `age`                                IS 55
        `paramedical`                        IS FALSE
        `entitled to a mother's position`    IS FALSE
        `school in the reform`               IS TRUE
        `substitute in weekly hours`         IS FALSE
        `placed in the placement system`     IS TRUE)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `an existing teacher of 55 gets two age bands`

-- The reading adopted: the band that opens at 55 governs 55 (4.4.2 read as
-- 50 up to 55).
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the age-hours reduction` t IS
    BRANCH IF t's `age` AT LEAST 55 AND `an existing teacher` t THEN `work week` 3 1 0
           IF t's `age` AT LEAST 50 THEN `work week` 2 0 0
           OTHERWISE `work week` 0 0 0

-- 4.4.2-4.4.4: the base after the reduction.
#ASSERT `total hours` (`work week` 23 4 9) MINUS 2 EQUALS 34
#ASSERT `total hours` (`work week` 23 4 9) MINUS 4 EQUALS 32
#ASSERT `total hours` (`work week` 23 3 10) EQUALS 36

-- akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4/p2 Points to the age-hours work-week tables on the web; no rule.
-- akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4/p3 The heading "the work week of principals and first deputies"; the rules follow.

-- 4.4.5: a principal and first deputy where the reform is applied work
-- exactly 100%, 5 days a week. 4.4.6: the principal's week is 40 hours;
-- in regular education the principal teaches 6-9 frontal hours by the
-- school's complexity (the table); 4.4.7: the Ministry sets the complexity
-- yearly. 4.4.8: the first deputy's week is 40 hours, 9-11 frontal hours
-- by the table.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-5
`the principal's position` MEANS 100%

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-6 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-6/t1 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-7
GIVEN `complexity` IS A NUMBER @desc the school's complexity level, 1 to 4, set yearly by the Ministry (4.4.7)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the principal's frontal hours` `complexity` IS
    BRANCH IF `complexity` EQUALS 1 THEN 9
           IF `complexity` EQUALS 2 THEN 8
           IF `complexity` EQUALS 3 THEN 7
           OTHERWISE 6

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-8 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-8/t1
GIVEN `complexity` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the first deputy's frontal hours` `complexity` IS
    IF `complexity` AT MOST 2 THEN 11 ELSE 9

`principals and first deputies work 40 hours` MEANS 40

-- The tables keep to the ranges the clauses state (6-9 and 9-11).
#ASSERT all (GIVEN c YIELD `the principal's frontal hours` c AT LEAST 6 AND `the principal's frontal hours` c AT MOST 9) (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN c YIELD `the first deputy's frontal hours` c AT LEAST 9 AND `the first deputy's frontal hours` c AT MOST 11) (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4)

-- 4.4.9: a second or later deputy works a teacher's week, doing the
-- deputy's work in the individual hours.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-9
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `works a teacher's week` t IF
    (NOT t's `role` EQUALS `a principal`) AND (NOT t's `role` EQUALS `a first deputy principal`)

-- 4.4.10: a principal or first deputy entitled to a mother's position may
-- take 2.5 stay hours off, and no frontal hours. 4.4.11: at 50 and above,
-- 2 weekly hours off the non-frontal hours, position and pay unchanged.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-10
`a principal mother's stay hours off` MEANS 2.5

@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-11
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a principal's age hours off non-frontal work` `age` IS
    IF `age` AT LEAST 50 THEN 2 ELSE 0

-- 4.4.12: a teacher appointed principal or first deputy stops working in
-- the upper division and works the whole position (40 hours) in the junior
-- high.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-11/p2
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `whole position in the junior high` t IF
    t's `junior-high position` EQUALS t's `total position`

-- F-2013-14_tashad_01-e: who approves employment above a full position.
-- 2ג ¶6 sends every request above 106% to the conditions-of-service
-- department at headquarters; 4.2.3 gives the approval of employment above
-- 100% to the district personnel managers, and 4.2.4 only what passes 42
-- hours to the head of the senior division. A request for 110%, within 42
-- hours, has two approvers.
`a teacher asking for 110%` MEANS
    `junior-high teacher` WITH
        `role`                               IS `a teacher`
        `prior teaching seniority recognised` IS TRUE
        `seniority years`                    IS 12
        `academic`                           IS TRUE
        `teaching certificate`               IS TRUE
        `completed internship successfully`  IS TRUE
        `signed the undertaking`             IS FALSE
        `junior-high position`               IS 1.1
        `total position`                     IS 1.1
        `number of schools`                  IS 1
        `age`                                IS 40
        `paramedical`                        IS FALSE
        `entitled to a mother's position`    IS FALSE
        `school in the reform`               IS TRUE
        `substitute in weekly hours`         IS FALSE
        `placed in the placement system`     IS TRUE

`a request for 110% within 42 hours` MEANS
    `extra-hours request` WITH
        `subject in demand`       IS TRUE
        `shortage in the area`    IS FALSE
        `remote locality`         IS FALSE
        `extra hours all frontal` IS TRUE
        `hours a day`             IS 8
        `hours a week`            IS 39.6

`2ג and 4.2.3 name different approvers for 110%` MEANS
    NOT (`who approves under 2ג` `a teacher asking for 110%` FALSE
         EQUALS `who approves` `a request for 110% within 42 hours`)
#ASSERT `2ג and 4.2.3 name different approvers for 110%`

-- The reading adopted: 2ג's headquarters approval for an owner's employee
-- above 106%, as the clause written for owners' employees; 4.2.3 for
-- 100%-106%, and 4.2.4 above 42 hours.

§§ `5. מקדמות השכר`

-- 5.1: in the first stage the teachers whose Ofek grade is not yet set get,
-- besides their present salary, an advance computed on it, on these
-- components; ¶2: for the junior-high fraction only, from the joining date;
-- the owner computes and pays it as "מקדמת אופק חדש". ¶3-¶6: the rates.
DECLARE `salary component` IS ONE OF
    `combined salary`
    `the '87 supplement`
    `the '94 supplement`
    `the 2001 supplement`
    `the 2008 supplement`
    `split-day allowance`
    `in-service training allowances`
    `double-degree allowance`
    `the 2011 supplement`
    `another component`

@ref akn:art_5__para_5-1 akn:art_5__para_5-1/p2
GIVEN c IS A `salary component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the advance base` c IF
    NOT c EQUALS `another component`

DECLARE `component paid` HAS
    `component`     IS A `salary component`
    `amount paid`   IS A NUMBER

-- The four rows as printed: teachers who are not principals or first
-- deputies 27%; interns 22%; first deputies 20%; principals 15%.
DECLARE `advance row` IS ONE OF
    `teachers who are not principals or first deputies`
    `interns`
    `first deputies`
    `principals`

@ref akn:art_5__para_5-1/p3 akn:art_5__para_5-1/p4 akn:art_5__para_5-1/p5 akn:art_5__para_5-1/p6
GIVEN row IS AN `advance row`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the rate the row prints` row IS
    CONSIDER row
    WHEN `teachers who are not principals or first deputies` THEN 27%
    WHEN `interns`        THEN 22%
    WHEN `first deputies` THEN 20%
    WHEN `principals`     THEN 15%

GIVEN row IS AN `advance row`, r IS A `role in the junior high`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the row covers` row r IF
    CONSIDER row
    WHEN `teachers who are not principals or first deputies` THEN (NOT r EQUALS `a principal`) AND (NOT r EQUALS `a first deputy principal`)
    WHEN `interns`        THEN r EQUALS `an intern`
    WHEN `first deputies` THEN r EQUALS `a first deputy principal`
    WHEN `principals`     THEN r EQUALS `a principal`

`the advance rows` MEANS
    LIST `teachers who are not principals or first deputies`, `interns`, `first deputies`, `principals`

GIVEN r IS A `role in the junior high`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the advance rates the rows give` r IS
    map (GIVEN row YIELD `the rate the row prints` row)
        (filter (GIVEN row YIELD `the row covers` row r) `the advance rows`)

-- F-2012-13_tashag_03-c: an intern is a teaching employee who is not a
-- principal or first deputy, so two rows price the intern.
`an intern has two advance rates` MEANS
    `the advance rates the rows give` `an intern` EQUALS LIST 27%, 22%
#ASSERT `an intern has two advance rates`

-- The reading adopted: the row that names interns governs them.
GIVEN r IS A `role in the junior high`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the advance rate` r IS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `an intern`                THEN 22%
    WHEN `a first deputy principal` THEN 20%
    WHEN `a principal`              THEN 15%
    OTHERWISE 27%

@export default The monthly "Ofek Hadash advance" an owner pays a junior-high teaching employee under circular תשע"ד/1, section 5 (the 27% was raised to 30% by circular תשע"ד/3)
GIVEN t IS A `junior-high teacher` @desc the employee
      `components` IS A LIST OF `component paid` @desc the present salary's components (not under Ofek Hadash terms) for the junior-high fraction
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Ofek Hadash advance` t `components` IS
    `the advance rate` (t's `role`)
    TIMES sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD IF `in the advance base` (c's `component`) THEN c's `amount paid` ELSE 0) `components`)

-- 5.2: from September to December, until the owners report list ב to the
-- district treasuries, owners entitled to union-hours funding are
-- reimbursed by advances (subject 15 in the payments system). 5.3: once the
-- placement, the grades and list ב are complete, the school's profile is
-- set and the Ministry funds the approved union hours of Ofek teachers
-- placed in the system. School months: September = 1, December = 4.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-2 akn:art_5__para_5-3
GIVEN `school month` IS A NUMBER, `list ב reported` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reimbursed by advances` `school month` `list ב reported` IF
    `school month` AT MOST 4 AND NOT `list ב reported`

§§ `6. שעון הנוכחות`

-- 6.1.1: a time clock is installed and teachers report their hours on it;
-- 6.1.3: until it is installed, reporting is manual.
@ref akn:art_6/p1 akn:art_6/p3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `ofek action`
DECIDE `the time clock` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `install a time clock`
    HENCE (PARTY `the teaching employee`
           MUST  `report working hours by the clock`)

-- 6.1.2: hours count from the clock-in, not before 7:45 (hours as decimals:
-- 7.75 = 7:45).
@ref akn:art_6/p2
GIVEN `clock-in time` IS A NUMBER @desc the time of day of the clock-in, in hours (7.75 = 7:45)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours count from` `clock-in time` IS
    max `clock-in time` 7.75

-- 6.1.4: the owner must pay and deduct salary by the clock reports, after
-- checking the absence certificates (sickness, mourning …), by the rules.
-- Monthly: within the month the report covers.
@ref akn:art_6/p4
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `ofek action`
DECIDE `pay and deduct by the clock` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `pay and deduct by the clock reports`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST  BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשע\"ד/1, 6.1.4: the owner pays and deducts salary by the time-clock reports"

-- akn:art_6/p5 6.1.5: the clock instructions are on the web; no rule.
-- akn:art_7 The contact line for questions; no rule.
-- akn:conclusions The greeting and the signature; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1 Annex א as the corpus has it: only the tail of its title (the undertaking form of a non-academic teacher); its content is missing from the corpus text.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1 Annex ב as the corpus has it: only the tail of its title (owners' employees in the official junior highs); its content is missing from the corpus text.

-- Examples; the teacher and the salary components are illustrations.
`Dana, a new teacher` MEANS
    `junior-high teacher` WITH
        `role`                               IS `a teacher`
        `prior teaching seniority recognised` IS FALSE
        `seniority years`                    IS 0
        `academic`                           IS TRUE
        `teaching certificate`               IS TRUE
        `completed internship successfully`  IS TRUE
        `signed the undertaking`             IS FALSE
        `junior-high position`               IS 0.6
        `total position`                     IS 0.6
        `number of schools`                  IS 1
        `age`                                IS 28
        `paramedical`                        IS FALSE
        `entitled to a mother's position`    IS FALSE
        `school in the reform`               IS FALSE
        `substitute in weekly hours`         IS FALSE
        `placed in the placement system`     IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the position the reform governs` `Dana, a new teacher` EQUALS 0.6
#ASSERT `total hours` (`the full-position work week` `Dana, a new teacher`) EQUALS 36
#ASSERT `total hours` (`the work week for the position` `Dana, a new teacher`) EQUALS 21.6
#ASSERT `the minimum position` `Dana, a new teacher` EQUALS 50%
#ASSERT `a non-academic joins` `a non-academic with thirty years`
#ASSERT `the Ofek Hadash advance` `Dana, a new teacher` (LIST `component paid` `combined salary` 5000, `component paid` `the 2011 supplement` 300, `component paid` `another component` 700) EQUALS 1431
#ASSERT `entitled to salary differences` 2012 2016
#ASSERT NOT `entitled to salary differences` 2014 2017.5
#ASSERT `hours count from` 7.5 EQUALS 7.75
`a forty-hour request` MEANS
    `extra-hours request` WITH
        `subject in demand`       IS TRUE
        `shortage in the area`    IS FALSE
        `remote locality`         IS FALSE
        `extra hours all frontal` IS TRUE
        `hours a day`             IS 8
        `hours a week`            IS 40

#ASSERT `who approves` `a forty-hour request` EQUALS `the district personnel managers`
#ASSERT `may be approved above a full position` `Dana, a new teacher` `a forty-hour request`

#TRACE `the owner's tasks` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `locate the teachers who meet the conditions` AT 0
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `send updated data to open or update a file` AT 1
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `employ by the Ofek work week` AT 1
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `send the salary interface to the conversion centre` AT 2
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education` DOES `approve joining and set the grade` AT 3
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay salary by the grade from joining` AT 4
#TRACE `pay and deduct by the clock` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `pay and deduct by the clock reports` AT 1
